/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261106071056\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics PDF pipeline)
/Keywords (polycrisis resilience\054 systemic resilience\054 crisis compounding\054 interconnected risks\054 resilience capacity\054 recovery gap\054 institutional capacity\054 fiscal space\054 adaptive social protection\054 disaster risk finance\054 vulnerability reduction\054 economic resilience)
/ModDate (D\07220261106071056\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (Between 2020 and 2026 the world absorbed a pandemic\054 the sharpest commodity\055price shock in half a century\054 the warmest years on record\054 a surge in armed conflict and a debt squeeze across the developing world\056 These were not separate events\072 each travelled through food\054 energy\054 finance\054 health and politics\054 and each arrived before societies had recovered from the last\056 This report\054 part of the H Heuristics Polycrisis Resilience series\054 asks which capacities let countries withstand\054 recover from and reduce their vulnerability to crises that compound\054 and where those capacities are missing\056)
/Title (Polycrisis Resilience 2026\072 Capacity\054 Clustering and the Recovery Gap across 166 Countries)
/Trapped /False
